  "codeFindings": [
    "RC5 runtime_liveness still rebuilds validated prefixes from store.readAll at its production callers; held successor uses the existing selectRuntimeEventPrefixFromStore owner.",
    "RC5 native_work_reacquisition has two callers of authenticateNativeInstructionAssemblyBasis. That wrapper first calls the owned authenticator, then materializes the complete history and constructs a validated prefix. Held successor calls authenticateOwnedNativeInstructionAssemblyBasis and removes the expanding adapter.",
    "These four implicated Product source files are byte-identical between RC4 and RC5; the later held successor changes them. RC5 Product code delta from RC4 is event_body_encoding.ts, event_store.ts, gtl/default_library.ts and product/contracts.ts."
  ],
  "functionalInterpretation": [
    "Actual current-state acquisition supports correct resumption/replay and binds the actual execution context.",
    "Input/install/worksite checks support exact code/input identity and stale/change/refusal detection at their true boundaries.",
    "The selector delegates a next-step choice; it is not coding work.",
    "Repeated expansion/reconstruction of an unchanged already-owned value provides no additional semantic guarantee when equivalent consumers can use the existing owner-held value."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "These are event/command boundary wall intervals, not per-function CPU profiles.",
